From c3a22698b86364d5f244064f1689e5cd18ff80c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:03:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mac/vulkan: show frames without waiting for the vsync with
 --macos-display-sync

In a window, macOS composites the layer at its own refresh whatever the
layer does: a frame presented without waiting for the vsync first
(displaySyncEnabled off) reaches the screen a frame or two sooner,
without tearing. --vulkan-swap-mode=immediate did that, but only when
the swapchain is made and in full screen too, where macOS may show the
layer directly and it can tear. --macos-display-sync=no turns the wait
off, fullscreen keeps it only in full screen; both at runtime, so a
script can ask for it while the input has to show quickly.

--macos-latency-log logs the frames enqueued to the sample buffer
layer as they're enqueued (sb=1): the layer doesn't say when it shows
them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
