@@ -7297,6 +7297,13 @@ them.
     ``afp_input_seq``; the VO then turns the view by the later gestures itself before it draws,
     and draws as each comes in, until the script's values come.
 
+``--macos-display-sync=<auto|no|fullscreen>``
+    Whether the Metal layer waits for the display's vsync to show a frame (``auto``: as
+    ``--vulkan-swap-mode`` says, waiting unless it's ``immediate``). ``no`` shows each frame as it
+    comes; in a window macOS composites it at its next refresh all the same, a frame or two sooner
+    than waiting for the vsync first, but in full screen (where macOS may show the layer directly)
+    it can tear. ``fullscreen`` waits only in full screen. Can be changed at runtime.
+
 ``--macos-latency-log=<yes|no>``
     Logs, for each frame shown through the swapchain, how long ago the input it shows came in
     (default: no): a line ``frame=<n> applied=<t> newest=<t> begin=<t> drawable=<t> submit=<t>
@@ -7306,7 +7313,9 @@ them.
     ``--glsl-shader-opts`` as ``afp_input_time`` (the gestures' script messages carry their event's
     time last); ``newest`` the newest input event when the VO began drawing it, ``begin`` then,
     ``drawable`` when the frame got the Metal layer's drawable, ``submit`` when it went to the
-    swapchain and ``shown`` when it was on screen (0: never).
+    swapchain and ``shown`` when it was on screen (0: never). Frames enqueued to the sample buffer
+    layer (``--macos-sample-buffer-layer``) are logged as they're enqueued, with ``shown=0 sb=1``:
+    the layer doesn't say when it shows them.
 
 ``--macos-latency-test=<0-1000>``
     Makes up a two-finger scroll of 4 points this many times a second, a second to the right and a
